  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nIssued 319 AM MDT WED OCT 14 2026\nwill continue warmer than normal temperatures, potentially 10 to 15 \ndegrees above normal, on Saturday. A northwest shortwave and \nassociated dry cold front on Sunday will help drop temperatures a \nfew degrees, but will still be 5 to 10 degrees above normal. On \nSunday, our area will come under a strong southwest flow ahead of an \nincoming Pacific upper low from the Gulf of Alaska. This flow will \nkeep Monday slightly warmer than normal but with increasing high \nclouds from the west. Tuesday through Wednesday, there is \nconsiderable guidance uncertainty over the upper low's movement \npattern as it nears our area. For now, Tuesday through Wednesday \nwill potentially see cooler than normal temperatures and \nprecipitation chances over most of the area.",
